<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lublin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lublin is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. It gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a>, agreed there in 1569, which joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> into a single <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. The city was an important commercial and political centre of the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lublin.jpg" alt="Lublin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kanion · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lublin_Panorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
